  "name": "redb",
  "description": "A high-performance, ACID-compliant embedded key-value store implemented in pure Rust using a copy-on-write B-tree architecture. It provides multi-version concurrency control (MVCC) for non-blocking concurrent access and features a zero-copy API for efficient data retrieval. The system is designed for crash safety and portability, incorporating advanced storage techniques such as buddy allocation and savepoint-based recovery.",
